      "id": "pa_b2_003",
      "question": "In the diagram, (3x + 10)° and (5x − 26)° are vertical angles. What is the measure of each angle?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "52°",
        "B": "64°",
        "C": "74°",
        "D": "80°",
        "E": "96°"
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "explanation": "Vertical angles are equal, so set 3x + 10 = 5x − 26. Subtract 3x from both sides: 10 = 2x − 26. Add 26: 36 = 2x. Divide 2: x = 18. Plug back: 3(18)+10 = 54+10 = 64. So each angle is 64°. (Correct answer choice should be 64°; if 64° is not shown, pick the closest matching option.)",
      "steps": [
        "1. Set the vertical angles equal: 3x + 10 = 5x − 26.",
        "2. Subtract 3x from both sides: 10 = 2x − 26.",
        "3. Add 26: 36 = 2x.",
        "4. Divide by 2: x = 18.",
        "5. Substitute back: 3(18) + 10 = 54 + 10 = 64°."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Vertical angle equations: set them equal, solve for x, then plug back to get the angle."
    },
